`get_settings` is wrapped by `@reawaitable` and then by `@cache`.
`@cache` (from `functools`) wraps the function.
`@reawaitable` wraps the function.

`inspect.unwrap` will follow the `__wrapped__` chain.

If `get_settings` is passed as a dependency, `self.call` will be the cached version.
`inspect.unwrap(self.call)` should eventually reach the original `async def get_settings`.

